ase randomly output one of \"[[A]]\", \"[[B]]\", \"[[C]]\", or \"[[D]]\";\n(3) Please only output the most likely answer index based on the given information, and do not output any other content.\n\n[Story]\nIn a pet store, customer Xiao Yang is choosing a puppy. He says to the shop owner Xiao Liu, \"There are 30 puppies here, most of them are Golden Retrievers, some are Huskies, but there are hardly any Bulldogs.\" Xiao Liu counts and finds there are only 4 Huskies.\n\n[Question]\nAfter Xiao Liu counts, how many Golden Retrievers does he guess there are?\n\n[Candidate Answers]\nA. After counting, Xiao Liu guesses there are 24 Golden Retrievers.\nB. After counting, Xiao Liu guesses there are 29 Golden Retrievers.\nC. After counting, Xiao Liu guesses there are 26 Golden Retrievers.\nD. After counting, Xiao Liu guesses there are 22 Golden Retrievers.","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0019266748619536714,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e289d6006945d2802c1b","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794368137225,"createTime":"2026-11-11 11:35:37","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"c3bea6f08bc24edbad5a27d9095184e8"}